1.0.1 2026-10-06
  - NEMAR redistribution of the authors' BIDS archive (Figshare 10.6084/m9.figshare.26131978.v3, ieeg_ieds_bids_final.zip, MD5 cdf392d5f92ba106b1f6794844147109). The archive is kept unchanged in sourcedata/. The 25 EDF files are byte-identical to the archive. The changes below are the only differences from the archive.
  - Fix A (validator error TSV_VALUE_INCORRECT_TYPE, 22 files): in sub-XX_task-sleep_events.json, trial_type had a "Levels" object that lists abbreviations (e.g. "Rt": "Right temporal"). The trial_type values themselves are free-text neurologist labels (e.g. "Rt sharp", "LEC LPHG mesial"), so the validator rejected every value that was not a key. The abbreviation list was moved, verbatim, into the trial_type "Description" text, and "Levels" was removed. No events.tsv value was changed. Files: sub-01..sub-18, sub-20, sub-21, sub-22, sub-25 (sub-19, sub-23 and sub-24 have no "Levels" and were not touched).
  - Fix B (validator error IEEG_ELECTRODES_REQUIRED, 7 participants): added sub-XX_electrodes.tsv and sub-XX_coordsystem.json for sub-08, sub-10, sub-11, sub-12, sub-13, sub-14, sub-15. The archive has no coordinates for these participants, so electrodes.tsv lists the referential contact names from the participant's channels.tsv (bipolar derivations excluded, matching the authors' electrodes.tsv for the other 18 participants) with x, y, z and size = n/a. coordsystem.json: iEEGCoordinateSystem "Other", iEEGCoordinateUnits "n/a", with a description saying that no coordinates are available. No coordinates were invented. Contacts listed: sub-08 14, sub-10 18, sub-11 15, sub-12 18, sub-13 12, sub-14 18, sub-15 17.
  - Fix C (validator warning TSV_COLUMN_TYPE_REDEFINED, 50 files): removed sidecar entries that only repeated the BIDS definition of standard columns and that the validator read as a string-typed redefinition: "name", "type", "units", "low_cutoff", "high_cutoff" and "sampling_frequency" from all 25 *_channels.json, and "onset" and "sample" from all 25 *_events.json. The non-standard columns (channels: side, soz_region; events: trial_type) keep the authors' descriptions.
  - Fix D (RecordingDuration reconciliation, 25 files): the source *_ieeg.json RecordingDuration used (n_samples - 1)/fs. It now holds the EDF header length n_records x record_duration (1000 Hz, 1-s records). Old -> new: sub-01 180.999->181.0; sub-02 180.999->181.0; sub-03 180.999->181.0; sub-04 180.999->181.0; sub-05 179.999->180.0; sub-06 180.999->181.0; sub-07 179.999->180.0; sub-08 179.999->180.0; sub-09 179.999->180.0; sub-10 206.999->207.0; sub-11 194.999->195.0; sub-12 229.999->230.0; sub-13 195.999->196.0; sub-14 200.999->201.0; sub-15 201.999->202.0; sub-16 175.999->176.0; sub-17 180.999->181.0; sub-18 180.999->181.0; sub-19 129.999->130.0; sub-20 60.999->61.0; sub-21 180.999->181.0; sub-22 290.999->291.0; sub-23 120.999->121.0; sub-24 179.999->180.0; sub-25 244.999->245.0. Total 4,603 s.
  - Fix E (validator warning TSV_ADDITIONAL_COLUMNS_UNDEFINED): participants.json now describes the "SOZ" column, using the authors' README wording ("SOZ: Seizure onset zone").
  - dataset_description.json: Name changed from "Depth IEDs" to the Figshare title (NEMAR requires a longer, descriptive name). License changed from "CC-BY-NC" to "CC-BY-NC-4.0" (most restrictive of the stated licences; the source gives no version; see README). Author spelling "Guy Gurevich" changed to "Guy Gurevitch", as on the Figshare record and in the paper. BIDSVersion changed from 1.7.0 to 1.10.0. Added HowToAcknowledge, Funding, EthicsApprovals (from Falach et al. 2024), SourceDatasets and GeneratedBy. The source "DatasetDOI" (10.6084/m9.figshare.26131978) identifies the Figshare original, not this copy, so it was moved to SourceDatasets/ReferencesAndLinks.
  - README.txt: the authors' text is kept verbatim. A "Redistribution on NEMAR" section was appended (source, licence statements and choice, ethics, recording notes, privacy review).
  - Added CHANGES (this file) and sourcedata/ieeg_ieds_bids_final.zip.

1.0.0 2024-12-30
  - Original release by the authors on Figshare (article 26131978, version 3).
